timertt (Timer Thread Template) is a small, template based, header only library
for C++11. It implements timer threads: thread which handles timers. timertt
has no external dependecies except standard C++11 library.

timertt was developed as part of SObjectizer[1] project but can be used as
standalone library.

timertt is distributed under 3-clauses BSD license (see LICENSE file).

Obtaining and Using
===================

There are three methods for obtaining timertt library source code.

1. Download minimal timertt archive from SObjectizer files section on
SourceForge[2]. This archive has name like timertt-1.2.X-headeronly.7z. Just
unpack this archive at appropriate location and add timertt folder to your
project's INCLUDE path.

2. Download full timertt archive from SObjectizer files section on
SourceForge[2]. This archive has name like timertt-1.2.X-full.7z. Just unpack
this archive at appropriate location and add timertt-1.2.X/include folder to
your project's INCLUDE path.

CMake users can consume timertt directly:

> add_subdirectory(timertt)
> target_link_libraries(your_target PRIVATE timertt::timertt)

Tests and samples are built with CMake:

> cmake -S . -B build-cmake
> cmake --build build-cmake --config Release
> ctest --test-dir build-cmake -C Release

Benchmarks are optional and can be enabled explicitly:

> cmake -S . -B build-cmake -DTIMERTT_BUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON

The old Ruby/Mxx_ru build files have been removed.

3. Export (or check out) timertt source code from Subversion repository on
SourceForge. For example:

> git clone <repository-url> timertt-1.2.5

Then add timertt-1.2.X/include to your project's INCLUDE path or consume the
`timertt::timertt` CMake target.

Like in previous method CMake can be used for building timertt tests and
samples.

API Reference manual can be built by Doxygen tool:

> cmake -S . -B build-cmake -DTIMERTT_BUILD_DOCS=ON
> cmake --build build-cmake --target timertt_docs

Generated documenation will be stored in build-cmake/docs/html.

Main Project Documentation
==========================

Main documenation for timertt library is on SObjectizer’s wiki[3] on
SourceForge.

Bug Reporting and Feedback
==========================

For bug reporting, proposals, discussions and stuff like that the appropriate
SObjectizer’s forums on SourceForge must be used [4],[5],[6]

